    "Combat.js",
    "Pickup.js",
    "Fx.js",
    "Hud.js"
  ],
  "controls": {
    "axis": "left stick / WASD",
    "Attack": "A / space (light combo)",
    "Heavy": "heavy attack action",
    "Dodge": "dodge action (roll)",
    "Jump": "rise again after the knight falls"
  },
  "systems": [
    "third-person camera",
    "three-step light combo plus a heavy swing",
    "dodge roll with invulnerability frames",
    "stamina economy",
    "wave director with rest phases",
    "telegraph/strike/recover enemy AI",
    "a boss with three ranged-by-distance attacks and a rage phase",
    "loot pickups",
    "HUD with health and stamina bars",
    "pooled combat FX",
    "brazier point lights"
  ],
  "engineNotes": {
    "notes": [
      "3D kit: kenney_nature_kit, dressed as a citadel instead of a valley -- the same pack supplies the walls (cliff cells), the bridges, the moat (water plates), the keep (stone platforms) and the statues.",
      "One colour per mesh object (Meshes.loadObj ignores mtllib/usemtl), so every tint is the model's face-dominant material mapped through this game's palette; see tools/biggames/kit3d.py.",
      "Motion is script-owned rather than Rigidbody3D/Collider3D.  The offline harness (tools/run_games.js) does not run PhysicsWorld3D, so a physics-driven combat game could not be verified before shipping; the scripts own position, and reach is resolved as a cone in Combat.js.",
      "Combat resolves in one place: Combat.strike(attacker, damage, reach, facing) hits whichever side the attacker is not on, so a Hollow, a Revenant, the Warden and the knight all share one definition of a hit.",
      "The engine keeps the four point lights nearest the camera (Renderer3D.setupLights), which is why the braziers are many and small rather than a few large ones."
    ]
  },
